In this lesson, you will have fun with the age-old question of,

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
to which parent the child looks the most similar?

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
To do this, you'll answer the question by using vector embeddings.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
You'll use a freely available image dataset,

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
in particular, one of the British royal family,

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
and use science to determine if Prince William looks more like King Charles or Princess Diana.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
It's simple and extensible enough for you to try on your own family pictures.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Let's have some fun!

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
We're going to build a facial similarity search system

10
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
to compute which parent looks most like their child.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
